    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 efficiency score makes him our premier play against Dustin May. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage (+14%), even with the slight drag created by the pitcher\u2019s elite hold capability. Following close behind are **Jackson Merrill** (72.12) and **Kyle Tucker** (70.41), both of whom offer elite production profiles. **Jackson Merrill** is positioned for a high-output day against Tyler Phillips, bolstered by a +13% platoon boost, while **Kyle Tucker** continues to be a staple of our offensive floor, providing consistent, high-value plate appearances that anchor our scoring potential regardless of the opposing matchup.\n\nStrategic platoon alignments have also elevated the profiles of **Heliot Ramos** (66.10) and **Miguel Vargas** (62.77). **Heliot Ramos** is particularly intriguing today; beyond his solid projection, he is a key target for stolen base opportunities given the slower delivery profile of his opposing starter. Conversely, the most difficult decision for the optimizer was leaving **Nasim Nunez** (42.36) on the bench. While **Nasim Nunez** brings the elite sprint speed we value for the SB category, the combination of a difficult matchup against Kyle Leahy and a negative park factor pushed his efficiency score just below the threshold for activation. We are keeping a close watch on the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Drake Baldwin** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**; should the confirmed lineups shift them out of their projected high-value spots, we may see further volatility in our daily efficiency ratings.",
